<p>Spirit Airlines ceased operations on Saturday, May 2, canceling all flights and beginning to wind down operations after last-minute talks with creditors and the White House failed. The U.S. budget carrier said “all flights have been cancelled, and customer service is no longer available,” leaving passengers and crew stranded around the United States, the Caribbean and Latin America. The company had been in bankruptcy since August 2025, its second bankruptcy in less than a year, and said a sharp rise in oil prices and other pressures had hurt its financial outlook. Sources described the failed rescue effort as a proposed $500 million federal bailout or government-backed rescue plan, while Spirit’s collapse followed a sharp rise in jet fuel costs tied to the Iran war. Spirit said Sunday that it had almost finished refunding customers for canceled flights. U.S. carriers including American, Delta, United, JetBlue, Southwest and Frontier offered reduced or “rescue” fares, added capacity on some routes, or opened hiring pathways for stranded Spirit workers.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/aLVlSvZIFns5afC4kN5ldrg8r9hcXZIzBN0Hu7zatLGkjxJQIeKUuydrkVEG3p7eaEmqtXzhOl0UWo2Q9t6vkxJRm1yB2Cnd6oR2q3zNmHx3' alt='A JetBlue plane taxis past grounded Spirit Airlines aircraft in Fort Lauderdale, Florida, after Spirit canceled all flights and began winding down.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Fuel shock: Spirit’s restructuring plan assumed jet fuel at $2.24 a gallon in 2026 and $2.14 in 2027, but La Jornada said the price had reached as much as $4.51 a gallon.</li><li>Airport disruption: At Chicago O’Hare, Terminal 2 screens told passengers Spirit was no longer operating, and CBS reported that some travelers arrived unaware and had to rebook on the spot.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>World Socialist Web Site: The publication argued that Washington’s decision not to rescue Spirit shifted the costs of the Iran war and energy shock onto workers. (<a href='https://www.wsws.org/en/articles/2026/05/04/mnml-m04.html'>World Socialist Web Site</a>)</li><li>Spirit workers: Former flight attendant Yeneshia Thomas said some employees first heard the news from their union before the company email. She described the closure as a blow to workers who had just finished shifts or remained on the road. (<a href='https://www.businessinsider.com/spirit-airlines-collapse-employees-jobs-workers-flight-attendant-2026-5'>Business Insider</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.wsws.org/en/articles/2026/05/04/mnml-m04.html'>Spirit Airlines collapses: 17,000 workers pay for Wall Street’s war on Iran</a> - wsws.org</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/united-states/spirit-airlines-says-most-customers-refunded-staff-returned-to-home-bases-after-sudden-shutdown'>Spirit Airlines says most customers refunded, staff returned to home bases after sudden shutdown</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.semafor.com/article/05/03/2026/spirit-closure-reflects-airlines-woes'>Spirit closure reflects airlines’ woes</a> - semafor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/may/03/spirit-airlines-customer-refunds'>Spirit Airlines says it has nearly finished refunding customers after shuttering</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://aviationsourcenews.com/spirit-airlines-shuts-down-end-of-an-era-for-the-budget-carrier/'>Spirit Airlines Shuts Down: End of an Era for the Budget Carrier</a> - aviationsourcenews.com</li><li><a href='https://unimedia.info/ro/news/141e5240e1d88941/compania-aeriana-care-si-a-anulat-toate-zborurile-si-intra-in-faliment-angajatii-raman-fara-loc-de-munca.html'>Compania aeriană care și-a anulat toate zborurile şi intră în faliment. Angajaţii rămân fără loc de muncă</a> - unimedia.info</li><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1997097/spirit-airlines-shuts-down-globally'>Spirit Airlines shuts down globally</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/chicago/news